  "dataNotes": [
    "Courses, credit hours and prerequisites come from the study plan. Suggested semesters come from the 2022 guidance plan.",
    "The 2022 guidance plan uses different codes for some courses: Foundation of Software Engineering (0103220 vs 0112303), Cybersecurity Law and Policy (0102301 vs 0112301), Cryptography & Computer Network Security (0112202 vs 0112304), Introduction to Artificial Intelligence (0102308 vs 0114208) and the capstone projects (0102490/0102491 vs 0112490/0112491). UniPath uses the study-plan codes and matches suggested semesters by course title.",
    "The study plan lists 0102320 as the prerequisite for Computer Forensics (0112302), but no course with that code is part of this degree. UniPath shows it as a note to confirm with your advisor instead of blocking the course.",
    "The study plan lists 0102431 as the prerequisite for Capstone Project II (0112491), but no course with that code is part of this degree. UniPath assumes Capstone Project I (0112490) comes first, as in the university's other engineering programs.",
    "The Cybersecurity study plan does not list a prerequisite for English 2 (0401121). UniPath follows the plan as written.",
    "The guidance plan calls 0107200 \"Discrete Structures\"; the study plan calls it \"Discrete Mathematics\". UniPath uses the study-plan title."
  ],
